Author: loop-bench <loop-bench@localhost>
Date:   Sat Nov 7 01:05:36 2026 +0100

    fix(orchestrator): call onError for non-error rejections

    The catch gated onError on error instanceof Error, so a thrown
    string, plain object or library-shaped rejection bypassed the hook
    entirely while still reaching the caller. Every rejection now fires
    onError: a non-Error is wrapped with a readable message and the
    original as its cause, an Error passes through as the same instance,
    and the caller still receives the original rejection unchanged.

    Fixes re-cinq/HALEngine#95

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>

